=========================================================
          MEDIATOR vs OBSERVER DESIGN PATTERN
=========================================================

BOTH CATEGORY:
Behavioral Design Pattern

Dono loose coupling dete hain.
Dono event-based lag sakte hain.
BUT core intent bilkul different hai.

=========================================================
1) ONE-LINE DIFFERENCE (MOST IMPORTANT)
=========================================================

MEDIATOR:
"Objects ke beech interaction ko centralize karta hai"

OBSERVER:
"State/event change hone par subscribers ko notify karta hai"

Golden memory trick:

Mediator = COORDINATION
Observer = NOTIFICATION

=========================================================
2) CORE INTENT DIFFERENCE
=========================================================

---------------------------------------------------------
MEDIATOR INTENT
---------------------------------------------------------
Many objects aapas me interact karte hain.

Goal:
Interaction rules ko ek central object me daalna.

Example:
- chat room
- ATC tower
- UI dialog controls
- booking orchestrator

Main idea:
Objects know only mediator
Objects don't know each other

---------------------------------------------------------
OBSERVER INTENT
---------------------------------------------------------
One object ki state change hoti hai,
baaki interested objects ko auto notify karna.

Example:
- YouTube subscribers
- stock price alerts
- event listeners
- notification service

Main idea:
Subject keeps list of observers
State changes → notify all

=========================================================
3) REAL LIFE ANALOGY
=========================================================

---------------------------------------------------------
MEDIATOR
---------------------------------------------------------
Office manager.

Employees directly ek dusre ko coordinate nahi karte.
Manager sabka work coordinate karta.

---------------------------------------------------------
OBSERVER
---------------------------------------------------------
YouTube channel.

New video upload hui → sab subscribers ko notification.

=========================================================
4) UML MINDSET
=========================================================

---------------------------------------------------------
MEDIATOR UML
---------------------------------------------------------

 User1 ----\
 User2 ----- > Mediator ----> routes interaction
 User3 ----/

Many-to-many interactions centralized

---------------------------------------------------------
OBSERVER UML
---------------------------------------------------------

              +------------------+
              |     Subject      |
              +------------------+
              | observers[]      |
              +------------------+
                 /      |      \
                /       |       \
               v        v        v
          Observer1 Observer2 Observer3

One-to-many notification model

=========================================================
5) DEPENDENCY FLOW DIFFERENCE
=========================================================

MEDIATOR:
Object -> Mediator -> Other Objects

OBSERVER:
Subject -> All Observers

Key:
Mediator = bidirectional communication possible
Observer = mostly one-way push from subject

=========================================================
6) WHO INITIATES COMMUNICATION?
=========================================================

MEDIATOR:
Any colleague initiates.
Mediator decides routing.

Example:
User sends message → mediator routes

OBSERVER:
Subject initiates.
Observers passive listeners.

Example:
Stock price changed → observers auto notified

=========================================================
7) RELATIONSHIP STYLE
=========================================================

MEDIATOR:
Many objects interacting with each other

Think:
many ↔ many
via central controller

OBSERVER:
One subject, many listeners

Think:
one → many

=========================================================
8) WHERE TO USE IN INTERVIEW
=========================================================

---------------------------------------------------------
USE MEDIATOR WHEN:
---------------------------------------------------------
- components coordinate
- workflow orchestration
- chat room
- dialog controls
- service coordinator
- air traffic control
- saga orchestrator

---------------------------------------------------------
USE OBSERVER WHEN:
---------------------------------------------------------
- event listeners
- pub-sub
- stock alerts
- UI updates
- cache invalidation
- metrics listeners
- order status notifications

=========================================================
9) EXAMPLE COMPARISON
=========================================================

---------------------------------------------------------
CHAT APP
---------------------------------------------------------

Mediator:
Users chatting with each other through chat room

Observer:
User subscribes to "online/offline status change" events

---------------------------------------------------------
E-COMMERCE
---------------------------------------------------------

Mediator:
Checkout workflow:
cart -> payment -> inventory -> shipping

Observer:
Order placed event:
- email service
- analytics
- loyalty points
- warehouse notification

=========================================================
10) CODE LEVEL DIFFERENCE
=========================================================

---------------------------------------------------------
MEDIATOR
---------------------------------------------------------
class User {
    IMediator* mediator;
};

user.send()
-> mediator.send()

---------------------------------------------------------
OBSERVER
---------------------------------------------------------
class Subject {
    vector<Observer*> observers;
};

subject.notifyAll()

=========================================================
11) INTERVIEW GOLD DIFFERENCE
=========================================================

MEDIATOR:
"communication complexity reduce"

OBSERVER:
"event notification distribute"

Best one-liner:
Mediator manages conversations.
Observer broadcasts events.

=========================================================
12) COMMON CONFUSION
=========================================================

Question:
"Dono me central object hota hai?"

Answer:
Yes, but purpose alag hai.

Mediator:
Decision making + routing + coordination

Observer:
Event registration + notification fanout

=========================================================
13) ADVANTAGES COMPARISON
=========================================================

MEDIATOR:
+ central rules
+ less coupling among peers
+ easy orchestration

OBSERVER:
+ dynamic subscribers
+ event driven
+ highly extensible
+ reactive systems

=========================================================
14) FAANG INTERVIEW ANSWER TEMPLATE
=========================================================

"Mediator is used to centralize interaction among multiple
peer objects and reduce many-to-many dependencies.

Observer is used for one-to-many event notification where
state changes in one object automatically notify all
registered listeners."

=========================================================
15) GOLDEN TAKEAWAY
=========================================================

Mediator = peer coordination
Observer = event subscription

If problem says:
'components talk to each other'
→ MEDIATOR

If says:
'state changed notify listeners'
→ OBSERVER

